1. Public: Members declared as public can be accessed from anywhere outside the class. They have no restrictions on their accessibility.

2. Private: Members declared as private can only be accessed within the same class. They cannot be accessed directly from other classes.

3. Protected: Members declared as protected can be accessed within the same package and any subclasses of the class. They cannot be accessed directly from other packages.

4. Default (or Package-private): Members declared without any modifier are considered default members. They can be accessed within the same package but not from other packages unless they are explicitly imported.

