 I have a many-to-many relationship between two entities, and I want to delete all related records when an entity is deleted. Is there any other way to achieve this?

Assistant: The `CascadeType.ALL` option in Hibernate's `@OneToMany` or `@ManyToMany` annotations specifies that when an entity is deleted, all associated entities should also be deleted.

Here's how you can use it:

```java
@Entity
public class Parent {
    @Id
    private Long id;

    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    private List<Child> children;
}
```

In this example, if you delete a `Parent`, its associated `Child` objects will also be deleted.

